Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?Phase=203=20firmware:=20epcs=5Fprogram=5Fpage?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20timing=20fix=20(partial=20=E2=80=94=20sectors=2010/12=20anom?=
 =?UTF-8?q?aly)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Bug observed in mode_t HW test (capture diag_phase3_mode_t_run3 +
external openFPGALoader dump): epcs_write_image wrote 368 KB into
EPCS slot 1 but only ~61% of bytes matched src.  Pattern was 'byte 1
of each page dropped' — chip received [buf[0], buf[2..255]] instead
of [buf[0..255]].

Root cause: in the per-page program loop, the iter-1
ctrl_shift_bytes pulse arrives too close to S_PAUSE entry (tick_cnt
ramp 0→3) — within the 'tick_cnt!=3' window where S_PAUSE doesn't
check the resume condition, so iter-1's pulse is lost.  Phase I3's
silicon-validated 8-byte case worked only because the per-iter
uart_puts created multi-µs spacing that hid the race.

Fix: insert CTRL_RESET pulse at start of epcs_program_page to clear
any stale flag_data_valid, plus an 8-cycle dead-loop between DATAIN
write and CTRL pulse in the inner loop.

Result (capture diag_phase3_mode_t_fix1 + dump fix1_epcs_dump.bin):
byte match 61.17% → 94.42%.  Sectors 8, 9, 11, 13 program byte-
identical to src.  Sectors 10 and 12 (EPCS 0xA0000 and 0xC0000)
still program a deterministic but wrong pattern (~38 mismatches per
page, no obvious shift/AND model).  Page 0 still fails entirely.

Open: residual sector-10/12 anomaly + page-0 failure.  Deterministic
(2 runs byte-identical), so not a race.  Cause unclear — patches
into a separate investigation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sw/stage2_loader/epcs.c | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sw/stage2_loader/epcs.c b/sw/stage2_loader/epcs.c
index 9a1777c..fe9f15d 100644
--- a/sw/stage2_loader/epcs.c
+++ b/sw/stage2_loader/epcs.c
@@ -130,6 +130,15 @@ int epcs_program_page(uint32_t addr, uint32_t len, const uint8_t *buf)
     if (len == 0) return 0;
     if (len > EPCS_PAGE_SIZE) return -1;
 
+    /* Clear any stale flag_data_valid from prior op (e.g. last
+     * byte_valid of an earlier WIP-poll cycle).  Without this the
+     * first iter's wait_dv could return immediately on stale flag,
+     * causing the iter-1 CTRL_SHIFT_BYTES pulse to fire while the
+     * wrapper is still mid-CMD-shift (pulse missed by S_PAUSE). */
+    *WB_AM_CTRL = CTRL_RESET;
+    for (volatile int d = 0; d < 32; d++) { }
+    wait_busy_clear(1000u);
+
     epcs_wren_pulse();
 
     /* First byte: addr + DATAIN + WRITE level (no SHIFT_BYTES yet). */
@@ -138,7 +147,13 @@ int epcs_program_page(uint32_t addr, uint32_t len, const uint8_t *buf)
     *WB_AM_CTRL   = CTRL_WRITE;
 
     /* Bytes 1..len-1: wait DV (wrapper paused after prior byte) →
-     * refill DATAIN → SHIFT_BYTES pulse (DV auto-clears on the pulse). */
+     * refill DATAIN → SHIFT_BYTES pulse (DV auto-clears on the pulse).
+     * The dead-loop between DATAIN write and CTRL pulse ensures that
+     * datain_reg is committed AND tick_cnt in S_PAUSE has reached 3
+     * before ctrl_shift_bytes asserts; matches the ~few-µs spacing
+     * that Phase I3's uart_puts inserted (which silicon-validated the
+     * 8-byte case).  Without the delay, iter 1's pulse arrives within
+     * 6-8 sysclks of byte_valid and falls in the tick_cnt<3 window. */
     for (uint32_t i = 1; i < len; i++) {
         if (!wait_dv(1000000u)) {
             *WB_AM_CTRL = 0;
@@ -146,6 +161,7 @@ int epcs_program_page(uint32_t addr, uint32_t len, const uint8_t *buf)
             return -2;
         }
         *WB_AM_DATAIN = buf[i];
+        for (volatile int d = 0; d < 8; d++) { }
         *WB_AM_CTRL = CTRL_WRITE | CTRL_SHIFT_BYTES;
     }
 
